WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:05.610
In A Song of Ice and Fire and Game of Thrones,
Tyrion Lannister encounters the mountain clansmen

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:10.110
of the Vale , “savage” warriors who live
as “bandits and outlaws” in the Mountains

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.490
of the Moon . The clansman threaten to kill
Tyrion at first , but he convinces them to

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:20.240
fight for him instead, promising gold , arms,
and the Vale itself . So the clansmen fight

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.400
for the Lannisters at the Green Fork and in
the Kingswood , they serve as guards for Tyrion

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.170
in King’s Landing , there’s some funny
banter about feeding manhoods to goats , but

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:33.320
by the start of Storm they go their separate
ways – some stay in the Kingswood, others

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.210
go home to the Vale . So the clansmen play
only a minor role in the story so far, but

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:42.560
there are actually some really cool theories
about them, one of which concerns Timett son

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.110
of Timett, a chief of the Burned Men.
The Burned Men are one of the clans that the

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.870
clansmen are divided into, along with the
Stone Crows, the Black Ears, and the Moon

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:56.059
Brothers . But the Burned Men stand apart
from the others , they’re feared by the

00:00:56.059 --> 00:01:00.660
other clans – because they have this custom
of burning away parts of their own bodies

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.140
to “prove their courage”, as a sort of
a coming-of-age manhood ritual. Most men burn

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:11.610
off a nipple, or a finger, or an ear, but
Timett put out his own left eye, and his fellows

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.610
were so impressed that they made him their
chief . We don’t learn much about Timett

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:20.020
as a person, apart from his ability to rip
out a man’s throat barehanded , but some

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:25.920
fans believe that he may be the rightful heir
to the Vale – potentially the ruler of one

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.410
of the Seven Kingdoms.
So the Lord of the Vale is currently Robert

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:35.060
– or Robin – Arryn , and he’s not expected
to live much longer , because he’s “weak

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.130
and sickly” , and because he’s being fed
dangerously high amounts of a drug called

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:43.820
sweetsleep under the orders of Littlefinger
. And Robert doesn’t have any children or

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:48.049
siblings, so “when he dies”, Lordship
of the Vale will be inherited by someone in

00:01:48.049 --> 00:01:52.930
his extended family. In Feast, Littlefinger
explains that since most of the Arryns are

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:57.909
dead, or joined the Faith, the heir to the
Vale after Robert is Harrold Hardyng – Robert’s

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:03.030
father’s sister’s daughter’s son. Littlefinger
plans to marry Sansa to Harrold in order to

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:07.400
win power over both the Vale and the North
– though in the show Sansa is married to

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.840
Ramsay Bolton, which is kind of a crazier
plan. Anyway Harrold, or Harry, is believed

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.840
to be the heir to the Vale – but Littlefinger
mentions that one of Harry’s mother’s

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.930
older sisters was “carried … off” by
the Burned Men . If that unnamed Waynwood

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:26.630
happened to have a legitimate child with one
of the Burned Men, that child would be heir

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:32.160
to the Vale ahead of Harry. Fans speculate
that Timett – the only named Burned Man

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:37.260
in the story – is that child, the rightful
Lord of the Vale after Robert.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:42.110
Admittedly, we’re not given any evidence
that this Waynwood woman ever had a son with

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:46.239
the Burned Men. But it’s certainly plausible,
and it could make a lot of narrative sense

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:50.610
for the mountain clans to take control of
the Vale. Because Tyrion promises the Vale

00:02:50.610 --> 00:03:01.519
to the clansmen , and we are all told that
“A Lannister always pays his debts” . And

00:03:01.519 --> 00:03:06.910
Tyrion is currently working with Daenerys
Targaryen, who intends to, eventually, invade

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:11.239
Westeros. Many fans believe that the Vale
could be an important location in Daenerys’

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:16.280
invasion because of its huge mountaintop castle,
the Eyrie, which is considered “impregnable”

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:21.690
– unless you have dragons – Daenerys could
fly right up there on Drogon . So if Daenerys

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.269
does invade the Vale, it would make a lot
of sense to use Tyrion’s relationship with

00:03:25.269 --> 00:03:29.800
the mountain clans to help take it – in
fact, Tyrion has already mentioned a plan

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:34.640
to use the clans against the Vale . Also,
we’re told that the clansmen, especially

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:39.459
Timett and the Burned Men, have become bolder
and more powerful since returning from King’s

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:43.700
Landing , so there’s little doubt they’d
be keen for an attack. So the pieces are all

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:48.400
here for Tyrion to use the clansmen against
the Vale, which could set the stage for Timett

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.540
to claim his rightful place as ruler of the
Vale.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.080
Of course, there are still big problems with
the idea. Firstly, Timett wouldn’t be considered

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.340
a legitimate heir unless his father – also
called Timett – and the Weynwood woman were

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.780
married – and we don’t know if the clansmen
even practice marriage. It’s possible for

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:09.640
a king or queen to legitimise Timett, though
technically an already-legitimate son like

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:14.209
Harry would still come first, so Harry might
have to die for Timett to legitimately be

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:18.650
the heir. Even if all that happens, it’s
very hard to imagine the Lords of the Vale

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:23.180
accepting a “savage” clansman as their
ruler – it could maybe be forced on them

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.900
whether they like it or not, but it’s hard
to see that working out in the long run. Finally,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.249
we don’t know if anyone in Westeros knows
about Timett’s possible parentage. And if

00:04:32.249 --> 00:04:38.249
they did, how could they prove it? Maybe Timett’s
mother is still alive, living among the mountain

00:04:38.249 --> 00:04:41.270
clansmen – perhaps she could attest to Timett’s
parentage.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:45.969
The bottom line is that it’s totally possible
that Timett son of Timett, or maybe some other

00:04:45.969 --> 00:04:50.379
unnamed Burned Man, is a descendent of the
Arryns. Whether he’ll ever be recognised

00:04:50.379 --> 00:04:54.969
as a legitimate heir to the Vale is less likely,
so maybe this’ll remain a little easter

00:04:54.969 --> 00:05:00.150
egg for the readers. Either way, it does seem
likely that Tyrion will use the clansmen against

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:04.279
the Vale, and Timett will presumably be a
part of that. So at the very least, we’ll

00:05:04.279 --> 00:05:08.240
probably get to see our favourite Burned Man
feeding manhoods to goats before the story

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.899
is done.
Thanks for watching. If you’d like to read

